<!--
  The Rinowa mark, on the launcher.

  ## Why this is not the icon it used to be

  It used to be four concentric circles while the status bar showed three open arcs. Two
  different marks for one app: the thing in the notification shade did not look like the
  thing on the home screen, which is the one place a mark has to be recognised instantly.

  This is the same drawing as ic_notification, scaled into the adaptive-icon safe zone.
  A circle is a shape a launcher imposes; it should not also be the mark.

  ## Geometry

  The 24dp notification artwork is placed with X = 54 + (x - 10.6) * 2.8 and
  Y = 54 + (y - 12) * 2.8, which centres it and leaves the outermost stroke inside the
  66dp guaranteed-visible area. Any launcher mask — circle, squircle, rounded square —
  clips background, never the mark.

  The three arcs carry increasing opacity outward-in, which the flat notification mark
  cannot do: a status bar icon is reduced to its alpha channel, so a graded version of it
  would silhouette differently. Here the shape is identical and only the weighting differs.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <path
        android:pathData="M44.5,43.4 Q33.8,54 44.5,64.6"
        android:strokeColor="#F2762F"
        android:strokeAlpha="0.45"
        android:strokeWidth="5.6"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000" />

    <path
        android:pathData="M59.3,33.8 Q44.5,54 59.3,74.2"
        android:strokeColor="#F2762F"
        android:strokeAlpha="0.75"
        android:strokeWidth="5.6"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000" />

    <path
        android:pathData="M74.2,27.1 Q55.1,54 74.2,80.9"
        android:strokeColor="#F2762F"
        android:strokeWidth="5.6"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000" />

</vector>
